  ex:l5-script-checking dct:references ex:l5-sm-qq, ex:l5-sm-pearson-density, ex:l5-sm-pearson-sum, ex:l5-sm-pearson-plot, ex:l5-sm-ks-code, ex:l5-sm-pearson-code .
  # Additional illustrations selected by thematic need, not by slide position.
  ex:l5-sm-process a cd:ScriptMaterial ; cd:position 3 ; cd:scriptResource ex:nn-process-media ; dct:title "One homogeneous nitrate control passes repeatedly through injection, separation, detection and reporting. The measurement path locates the contributions to variation."@en .
  ex:l5-sm-density-sample a cd:ScriptMaterial ; cd:position 6 ; cd:scriptResource ex:pc-density ; dct:title "A histogram of 1,000 simulated nitrate results and its generating Normal density share concentration axes. Between 9.9 and 10.1 mg/L, the observed sample fraction is 66.7%, compared with a model probability of about 68.27%."@en .
  ex:l5-sm-ecdf-plot a cd:ScriptMaterial ; cd:position 7 ; cd:scriptResource ex:p1-ecdf-start ; dct:title "The empirical CDF of 20 simulated nitrate results is compared with the generating Normal CDF. All 20 observations lie at or below 10.20 mg/L, giving empirical fraction 1 at that threshold; the model probability there is about 97.72%. Steps accumulate observed fractions, while the smooth curve accumulates model probability."@en .
  ex:l5-sm-normal-density a cd:ScriptMaterial ; cd:position 9 ; cd:scriptResource ex:pc-phi-chart ; dct:title "The standard-Normal density is symmetric about zero, where it reaches its maximum. The horizontal coordinate is standardized distance and the vertical coordinate is density per standardized unit."@en .
  ex:l5-sm-device-densities a cd:ScriptMaterial ; cd:position 10 ; cd:scriptResource ex:p1-normal-devices ; dct:title "Two Normal models share expectation 10.00 mg/L and the marked result 10.20 mg/L. Known SDs of 0.10 and 0.20 mg/L put that result two SD above the expectation for A and one SD above it for B."@en .
  ex:l5-sm-band-areas a cd:ScriptMaterial ; cd:position 11 ; cd:scriptResource ex:p1-normal-bands ; dct:title "The panels compare a one-sided upper 1% limit, about 10.233 mg/L, with a central two-SD band under the Normal model with expectation 10.00 mg/L and SD 0.10 mg/L. The central band contains about 95.45% of the probability, leaving about 4.550% across both tails."@en .
  ex:l5-sm-preparation a cd:ScriptMaterial ; cd:position 8 ; cd:scriptResource ex:lg-process-media ; dct:title "Path A reinjects one prepared control; path B repeats extraction, concentration and analysis on independent aliquots. The paths define different repeat experiments."@en .
  ex:l5-sm-logsample a cd:ScriptMaterial ; cd:position 9 ; cd:scriptResource ex:lg-saved-chart ; dct:title "The simulated complete-preparation sample contains 1,000 positive concentrations. Its long right tail includes 100 results above 15 ng/L; this is an observed fraction of this finite simulation."@en .
  ex:l5-sm-ratio-scales a cd:ScriptMaterial ; cd:position 10 ; cd:scriptResource ex:lg-scales-media ; dct:title "The concentrations 8, 10 and 12.5 ng/L have unequal linear gaps. Relative to 10 ng/L their natural log ratios have equal gaps on either side of zero."@en .
  ex:l5-sm-logtasks a cd:ScriptMaterial ; cd:position 11 ; cd:scriptResource ex:p1-log-tasks ; dct:title "The left panel shades the probability above 15 ng/L, about 8.826%; the right finds the concentration for an upper-tail rate of 5%, about 16.38 ng/L. Both use median 10 ng/L and dimensionless log SD 0.30."@en .
  ex:l5-sm-precision-process a cd:ScriptMaterial ; cd:position 6 ; cd:scriptResource ex:ic-process-media ; dct:title "The precision experiment repeats six independent nitrate measurements of one homogeneous sample. The reference repeatability SD, 0.10 mg/L, is known independently."@en .
  ex:l5-sm-series a cd:ScriptMaterial ; cd:position 7 ; cd:scriptResource ex:p1-series-chart ; dct:title "Three constructed six-result series share mean 10.000 mg/L. Their sample variances are A: 0.00316, B: 0.00748 and C: 0.01648 (mg/L) squared. Small horizontal offsets separate individual results within each group, including ties."@en .
  ex:l5-sm-size-comparison a cd:ScriptMaterial ; cd:position 8 ; cd:scriptResource ex:p1-variance-compare ; dct:title "The histograms compare variance estimates from 1,000 Normal series of 6 measurements with 1,000 series of 30 measurements on the same scale. Population SD remains 0.10 mg/L in both experiments. Increasing series size reduces the theoretical relative SD of the variance estimate from 63.25% to 26.26%; the simulated six-result series give 61.79%."@en .
  ex:l5-sm-square-transform a cd:ScriptMaterial ; cd:position 6 ; cd:scriptResource ex:ix-square-media ; dct:title "Squaring maps both signs of a standard-Normal value to the same nonnegative squared distance. The symmetric Normal density becomes a one-degree-of-freedom chi-square density."@en .
  ex:l5-sm-residual-squares a cd:ScriptMaterial ; cd:position 7 ; cd:scriptResource ex:ic-residual-media ; dct:title "The six nitrate residuals are divided by the independently known reference SD, squared and added. Their squared standardized values sum to 12; estimating the mean leaves five degrees of freedom."@en .
  ex:l5-sm-precision-tail a cd:ScriptMaterial ; cd:position 8 ; cd:scriptResource ex:ic-tail-media ; dct:title "The five-degree-of-freedom chi-square curve marks the upper 5% cutoff at 11.07 and the observed statistic at 12. The shaded upper probability beyond 12 is about 3.48%."@en .
  ex:l5-sm-student-flow a cd:ScriptMaterial ; cd:position 3 ; cd:scriptResource ex:dist-t-intro-flow ; dct:title "One complete Normal sample supplies both its mean and estimated standard error. The process contributes one studentized value per repetition."@en .
  ex:l5-sm-student-simulation a cd:ScriptMaterial ; cd:position 4 ; cd:scriptResource ex:dist-t ; dct:title "Studentized means from 1,000 repeated two-result Normal samples form the histogram. The Student reference has one degree of freedom; the standard-Normal curve gives a known-spread comparison."@en .
  ex:l5-sm-f-flow a cd:ScriptMaterial ; cd:position 5 ; cd:scriptResource ex:dist-f-intro-flow ; dct:title "Two independent Normal samples supply two estimated variances. Normalizing by the true variances and taking B/A contributes one F variable per sample pair."@en .
  ex:l5-sm-device-results a cd:ScriptMaterial ; cd:position 6 ; cd:scriptResource ex:rx-devices ; dct:title "Two independent constructed groups each contain six nitrate results. Sample SDs of 0.10 mg/L for A and 0.30 mg/L for B give the ordered sample-variance ratio B/A = 9. Small horizontal offsets separate individual results, including ties."@en .
  ex:l5-sm-qq-panels a cd:ScriptMaterial ; cd:position 7 ; cd:scriptResource ex:rev-qq-media ; dct:title "Both Q-Q panels use the Normal model with expectation 10 mg/L and SD 0.50 mg/L fixed before observing either five-result sample. Sample A lies close to the identity line; sample B bends toward its extreme upper observation."@en .
  ex:l5-sm-ks-panels a cd:ScriptMaterial ; cd:position 8 ; cd:scriptResource ex:rev-ks-media ; dct:title "The ECDFs and fixed Normal CDF (expectation 10 mg/L, SD 0.50 mg/L) use common concentration axes. Vertical gaps include both sides of each empirical jump; maximum distances are 0.144578 for A and 0.725747 for B."@en .
  ex:l5-sm-particle-counts a cd:ScriptMaterial ; cd:position 9 ; cd:scriptResource ex:rx-pearson ; dct:title "Observed counts for 100 particles in five fixed diameter categories are compared with expected counts 10, 20, 40, 20 and 10. The highlighted reference points show the fixed expectations."@en .
